Jody M Friese wrote in message ...

>What next? The obvious is to wish for Blessed Scrolls of Charging (which I
>haven't seen yet), for the wand as well as my markers. But what else do I
>need? I seem to have pretty good stuff to this point. Spellbook of Identify
>or Remove Curse? Frostbrand? Gauntlets of Dexterity? More markers? Will I
>need disintegration resistance (I have SDSM, so...)?

As for dsntgrtn res... better safe than sorry. Verily 'tis so. Eat a black dragon.

Since you have dry markers (assuming they have never been charged), 
it would be indeed great to get at least 2 blessed scrolls of charging from a
single wish. Sometimes you get lucky. With a charged marker, good luck,
good mental stats (iirc) and a pair of lenses on, wizards have a great (the best)
chance of writing a previously unknown scroll.

Do you have a wand of enlightenment ? (are your wands id'd?)
You could easily id lots of (uncursed) critical rings and
amulets with it. 

You could always try to search the chests and boxes in Valley
of Death before wishing for anything. Then, if you take the time
and if you have a /oPolymorph, you could polypile stuff in the
hope of producing a ?oCharging, markers or other nice stuff.
Polypiling spellbooks is risky, because the resulting books may
instantly become blank when you try to read them.

"A wish for a magic marker is always a good wish", sayeth a proverb.

Wizards don't really need a physical artifact weapon for close-quarters-
battle, other than Magicbane. Magic missile does nice damage to
all (most) enemies, especially if the spell bounces around.
However, Staff of Aesculapius comes to mind, since you're neutral...
but you may not want to risk losing a wish now that too many artifacts
already exist in the game.

GoD are usually wizard's favourite gloves (especially for a human!),
so wear and enchant them if you come by them.

Helm of Brilliance, especially when fully enchanted, is the best
helmet for a human wizard. 

As for curses... Magicbane protects you against 99% of them, 
but to be able to remove curses from _lots_ of items, Remove
curse comes in handy (an understatement).

>My Spellbook stash is currently on DLVL 20. Do I move it down? (I'll be due
>to re-read stuff soon.) Should I go up and try to finish the mines? 

If you don't mind travelling between levels, there's no great need
to move the spellbook stash.

The Mines' End contains a luckstone and perhaps other magical stones,
for the better or the worse. ID and bless the luckstone and keep it in your
main inventory.

The only greater danger in the Mines are possible polytraps, which may
possibly create horrible monsters, which, in turn, may possibly summon
more horrible creatures. But, these are mostly dangerous to unprepared
low-level charecters who venture down the Mines.

As for identifying... a b+oIdentify can't be a bad wish - identifying
previously unknown stuff and known wands' and other items' charges
is important. 

Then there are the matters of improving your AC (once you choose
your complete AK), your max hp (only partially solved by gaining levels),
your max str  etc. etc...  those I'll leave to others ...

